### u2worksheet06-gpimage04.gp
### Q4 solutions graph: g(t) = 0.5t^3 - 5.5t^2 + 14t - 90 (the shifted
### function whose sign answers "is the stock above $90"), root at t=10.
### Same underlying word problem as u2lesson06 Part 2 Q3, rebuilt here as
### this worksheet's own numbered figure. Regenerated with shading (item 7
### follow-up, see review-notes.md) -- generated by inequality_graph.py.
set terminal pngcairo size 460,420 enhanced font "Arial,12"
set output '../u2lessons-media/u2worksheet06-gpimage04.png'

set xrange [0.0:13.0]
set yrange [-120.0:160.0]

set xzeroaxis
set yzeroaxis

set xlabel "t"
set ylabel "y" rotate by 0
set grid

set xtics 1
set ytics 30
set mxtics 2
set mytics 2

unset key

f(t) = (0.5)*t**3 + (-5.5)*t**2 + (14.0)*t + (-90.0)

set style fill transparent solid 0.3 noborder
set style arrow 1 head filled size screen 0.02,20 lw 3 lc rgb "#3355bb"
set arrow 1 from 10.0,0 to 13.0,0 as 1

plot '-' using 1:2 with filledcurves closed lc rgb "#3355bb" notitle, \
     f(x) with lines lw 2.5 lc rgb "#3355bb" notitle, \
     '-' using 1:2 with points pt 7 ps 1.3 lc rgb "black" notitle
